{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.MayerThreeBodySign","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":25,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.neg_phi2_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.neg_phi2_pos","kind":"theorem","line":270,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.lean#L270-L274","doc":"The pair coefficient of the Mayer binding is positive on `(0,1)`: `−φᵀ₂ = 1 − f > 0`. With\n`phi3_pos` this is the alternation `(−1)^{n−1} φᵀ_n > 0` at `n = 2, 3`, and it is the sign\npattern the corpus already carries — `b₂ > 0`, `b₃ < 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.b3corpus_uniform_eq_mayerSign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.b3corpus_uniform_eq_mayerSign","kind":"theorem","line":264,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.lean#L264-L268","doc":"On uniform bonds this file's `b₃` is `MayerThreeBodySign.b3` with `P₃ = f³` — the same object,\nso `lt_of_b3_pos` and `b3corpus_neg` are about one quantity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.b3corpus_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.b3corpus_neg","kind":"theorem","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.lean#L254-L261","doc":"**No threshold.** The corpus's three-body cumulant is strictly negative for every bond triple\nin `(0,1)`, uniform or not, whatever the like-pair typing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.phi3_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.phi3_pos","kind":"theorem","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.lean#L238-L252","doc":"**The Ursell alternation at `n = 3`, strict.** For bond factors in `(0,1)` the third Ursell\nfunction is strictly positive: `φᵀ₃ = (1−f₁₂)(1−f₁₃) f₂₃ + (1−f₂₃)((1−f₁₂) + (1−f₁₃))`, a sum of a\nstrictly positive and a non-negative term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.restored_eq_neg_activity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.restored_eq_neg_activity","kind":"theorem","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.lean#L225-L230","doc":"**The restored alternation is the Mayer binding at negative activity.** Flipping the sign of\nthe third coefficient alone is exactly `z ↦ −z` in `−ln(Ξ/Ξ_free)`; no ensemble at positive\nactivity produces it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.restored","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.restored","kind":"def","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.lean#L220-L223","doc":"The 2026-08-30 \"restored alternation\" `b_T = (−1)^{|T|−1} φᵀ_T`: pair coefficients `−g`,\ntriple coefficient `+φᵀ₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.mayerBinding_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.mayerBinding_eq","kind":"theorem","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.lean#L211-L218","doc":"**Uniform minus.** The Mayer coefficients of the binding are `−φᵀ_T` at every order: the\npair coefficient `−g = 1 − f` (positive on `(0,1)`) and the triple coefficient `−φᵀ₃`. The corpus's\n`b₂ = −φᵀ₂`, `b₃ = −φᵀ₃` is this expansion, not a sign error in it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.mayerBinding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.mayerBinding","kind":"def","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.lean#L206-L209","doc":"The Mayer expansion of the log-derived binding `B = −α ln(Ξ/Ξ_free)` (in units of `α`):\n`−(U − Σ_i z_i)`, the free reference `Ξ_free = ∏(1 + z_i)` removed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.U","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.U","kind":"def","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.lean#L200-L204","doc":"The multilinear log of `Ξ_S(z) = Σ_{T ⊆ S} z^T Z_T` on a three-cluster:\n`U = Σ_T z^T φᵀ_T` (the exponential formula; verified symbolically in the probe). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.matching_defect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.matching_defect","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.lean#L192-L196","doc":"The matching defect is not zero: at uniform `f = 1/2` it is `3/4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.b4corpus_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.b4corpus_eq","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.lean#L182-L190","doc":"**Where the identity breaks.** The corpus's `b₄` is minus the fourth Ursell function **minus\nthe three perfect matchings** — the isolated-vertex-free spanning graphs on four vertices that\nare not connected. This is the closed form of the 2026-08-30 probe's \"matches neither `+φᵀ₄` nor\n`−φᵀ₄`, 200/200\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.b4corpus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.b4corpus","kind":"def","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.lean#L174-L180","doc":"The corpus's four-body cumulant, in the form `QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing.b4` uses:\n`W(1234) − Σ_{pairs} W − Σ_{triples} b₃(T)`, on the multiplicative binding. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.phi4_eq_connected_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.phi4_eq_connected_sum","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.lean#L158-L172","doc":"The cluster-property definition agrees with the connected-graph sum: the thirty-eight\nconnected spanning subgraphs of `K₄` (sixteen trees, fifteen with four edges, six with five,\nand `K₄` itself). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.phi4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.phi4","kind":"def","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.lean#L148-L156","doc":"The fourth Ursell function **defined by the cluster property**\n`Z_S = Σ_{π ∈ Π(S)} ∏_{B ∈ π} φᵀ_B` over the fifteen set partitions of a four-set: one of type\n`4`, four of type `3+1`, three of type `2+2`, six of type `2+1+1`, one of type `1+1+1+1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.Z4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.Z4","kind":"def","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.lean#L145-L146","doc":"Canonical partition function of a four-cluster: the product of its six bond factors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.b3corpus_uniform_closed_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.b3corpus_uniform_closed_form","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.lean#L137-L141","doc":"On uniform bonds `b₃ = 3f − 2 − f³ = −(1 − f)²(f + 2)`: the `2/3` threshold of\n`MayerThreeBodySign` is never reached once `P₃` is the bond product. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.boolean3_eq_phi3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.boolean3_eq_phi3","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.lean#L128-L135","doc":"**Why it holds at `n = 3`.** The Boolean inversion of the bond-multiplicative `Z` itself,\n`Z(123) − Z(12) − Z(13) − Z(23) + Z(1) + Z(2) + Z(3) − Z(∅)` with `Z = 1` on sets carrying no\nbond, is the sum over spanning edge sets with no isolated vertex. On three vertices every such\nedge set is connected, so it *is* `φᵀ₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.b3corpus_eq_neg_phi3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.b3corpus_eq_neg_phi3","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.lean#L122-L126","doc":"**The identity.** The corpus's three-body cumulant is exactly minus the third Ursell function\nof the Mayer variables — for every triple, uniform or not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.b3corpus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.b3corpus","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.lean#L116-L120","doc":"The corpus's connected three-body cumulant on a triangle of bond factors: the Boolean\n(inclusion–exclusion) inversion `W(123) − W(12) − W(13) − W(23)`, singletons carrying `W = 0`.\nThis is `QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing.b3` evaluated on the multiplicative binding. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.W","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.W","kind":"def","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.lean#L113-L114","doc":"The multiplicative assembly of `MayerThreeBodySign`: `W(S) = 1 − Z_S`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.cluster3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.cluster3","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.lean#L101-L109","doc":"**The cluster property at `n = 3`.** `Z_S = Σ_{π ∈ Π(S)} ∏_{B ∈ π} φᵀ_B` over the five set\npartitions of a three-set (`{123}`, three of type `2+1`, and `1+1+1`), with `φᵀ_{i} = 1`. This is\nthe defining relation of the Ursell functions, and it is what makes `φᵀ_T` the coefficient of\n`z^T` in `ln Ξ` (exponential formula). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.Z3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.Z3","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.lean#L97-L99","doc":"The canonical partition function of a three-cluster with bond factors `f_e`: the product of\nthe bond factors, which is the trace ratio `tr_M(atom)/tr_M(free)` by bond multiplicativity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.phi3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.phi3","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.lean#L93-L95","doc":"The third Ursell function: the four connected spanning graphs on three labelled vertices —\nthe triangle and the three paths. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.phi2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.phi2","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.lean#L90-L91","doc":"The second Ursell function: the single edge. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.mayer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.mayer","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UrsellPartitionFunctionB3.lean#L87-L88","doc":"The Mayer variable of a bond factor: `g = f − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}